{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuVr7LCPQ9VhdCsoEj8e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard or check that the panels render. I also haven't seen the rule run.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view has a `timestamp` field. It also has `response` (a string, so I filtered on `response.keyword`), `bytes`, `extension`, `geo.src` and `clientip`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-a98b9dad Web logs overview\" has 5 panels. You can open it at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-a98b9dad-web-logs-overview-dfdc208d7463`. The default time range is the last 7 days.\n- Total requests (a single number)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Requests by response code (pie chart)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar chart)\n- Top source countries (table)\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-a98b9dad 5xx spike\" (id `96c17f48-68b2-4528-84ce-a1ee00a26abc`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It runs every minute.\n- It counts documents whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over the last 5 minutes.\n- It fires when that count is above 10.\n- It has no action attached, so when it fires it only shows as an alert in Kibana. It won't send a notification anywhere.\n\nThe rule was created disabled, so I enabled it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1132,"cache_read_input_tokens":20527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1132},"output_tokens":480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"c2a4ca24-fccf-4a7d-92ef-d08a2cbefaef","timestamp":"2026-10-11T00:24:40.057Z","request_id":"req_011CfuVr7Amd31Uv4qwxvd3n"}
